    trace_spec_to_testcase_edges_not_produced_2026-11-06, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep7: reproduced (sspec_inventory source character/byte mapping mismatch; ch.len() returns characters - 5 for ab日本c - not bytes 9; extraction aborted with zero cases -> zero edges). Shared root cause with the sibling trace_specs_preexisting_failures row (its other failures already fixed by other lanes). Fix: src/app/traceability/extract/sspec_inventory.spl:83 byte_offset += ch.byte_len() - one line. Impact scale: 1508 test/03_system specs contain non-ASCII, so the pipeline produced no edges for them. Verification: sspec_inventory_spec 9/9 (was 7/8, +1 new non-ASCII case with byte-span assertions); end-to-end probe over the real pipeline entry build_sspec_trace_request_single_owner confirms planned cases with exact selectors and byte spans; neighbours codec 7/7, preparation 6/6, run_plan 9/9, run_request_codec 4/4, sspec_run_request 9/9, snapshot_pipeline 7/7, snapshot_facts 6/6, push_refs 10/10, snapshot_delta 9/9. Residuals: native re-verification + the doc's full-pipeline grant step need a native-binary host; the closed-profile multi-import rejection is a separate documented contract. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/app/traceability/sspec_inventory_spec.spl prevention=src/app/traceability/extract/sspec_inventory.spl"
